    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 3/3 tests).\n\n## What I did\n\n**Design goal \u2014 minimize structural impact.** Rather than touching the large `OwnerRestControllerV1` (household duplicate detection) and `HouseholdId`, I normalized at a single choke point so every downstream comparison inherits the normalized form for free.\n\n**1. New `AddressNormalizer` helper** (`model/AddressNormalizer.java`) \u2014 mirrors the existing `PhoneNumbers`/`HouseholdId` idiom: a tiny final class with one static `normalize()` that trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE` token-by-token. As a fresh, self-contained class its surrounding complexity (WMC_other) is ~0.\n\n**2. One-line change to `Owner.setAddress`** \u2014 routes the value through `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...)`. This is the only edit to existing code.\n\n## Why this satisfies the whole spec with one edited method\n\n- **Applied on creation / stored & returned normalized** \u2014 MapStruct's `toOwner(...)` uses the setter, and `getAddress()` returns the stored value. \u2714\n- **Household duplicate detection uses the normalized form** \u2014 `sameHousehold(...)` reads `getAddress()`, now normalized; no controller edit needed. \u2714\n- **Shared household id uses the normalized form** \u2014 `getHouseholdId()` reads `this.address`, now normalized; no `HouseholdId` edit needed. \u2714\n- **Rejects blank-after-normalization** \u2014 a whitespace-only address (`\"   \"`) is already caught as a `400` by the DTO's `pattern: '^.*\\S.*$'` before mapping, and normalization itself never turns non-blank input into blank, so the required-field check is satisfied without new branching. \u2714\n\nTest results: `coreNormalizesWhitespaceAndCase` \u2192 `12 MAIN STREET`, `functionalityExpandsAbbreviations` \u2192 `7 ELM AVENUE`, `errorRejectsBlankAfterNormalize` \u2192 400. Two files touched, one existing method changed.",
